      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey so i just updated the A records for a client site but the new IP isnt showing up anywhere. it’s been like two hours and it’s still pointing to the old server on my end. why does this take so long? is there some kind of delay in the system?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There may be a propagation delay, as DNS updates can take some time to be fully propagated across the global DNS system. Typically, the TTL (Time to Live) value affects this delay. If you've refreshed the A record correctly, it usually resolves within 24 to 48 hours, but sometimes it can take longer. It's also possible that the system is caching the old IP. You can use online tools like DNS Checker to verify the propagation and ensure your A record update is fully propagated worldwide.",
